📁 File I/O in Python
What is File I/O?

File I/O = File Input / Output

It means:

Input → Reading data from a file

Output → Writing data to a file

Until now, your programs:

Took input from the user

Printed output to the console

With file I/O:

Data stays saved even after the program ends ✅

You can process large datasets

You can build real applications
--------

************
Python can be used to perform operations on a file. (read & write data)


Types of files
1) Text files : .txt, .docx, .log
2) Binary files : .mp4 , .mov, .png, .jpeg

Open, read, and close file

We have to open a file before reading or writing

f = open("file_name", "mode")

file_name = sample.txt, demo.txt
mode = read mode, write mode

If we do not specify the mode, the python consider it as read by default.


data = f.read()
f.close()
**************

Modes (Very Important)
Mode	Meaning
"r"	Read (default)
"w"	Write (overwrites file)
"a"	Append (adds to file)
"x"	Create new file (error if exists)
"b"	Binary mode
